; The mutation loop: the parent process of a mutation run, above the
; core. It installs itself into the core's Registry at module load, and
; that self-install is the whole mechanism — core names no loop, so the
; stanza that links this library is what arms mutation, explicit and
; greppable. A standalone suite adds windtrap.mutation next to windtrap;
; the inline runner carries it through ppx_windtrap.runtime's own
; dependency (see ppx/runtime/dune).
;
; -linkall is load-bearing: no module anywhere references Mutate_loop,
; so without it the linker would drop the unit from every closure and
; the self-install would never run — WINDTRAP_MUTATE would silently
; select a plain run. The flag marks the archive so any binary that
; links the library loads the unit. test/mutate_loop is the fence.
;
; No mutation stanza, deliberately: a mutant armed inside the judging
; process hangs rather than surviving, so this library must never
; become instrumentable — mutate_loop.ml's [@@@mutate exclude_file]
; states the same intent in-file. The core measures its own coverage
; and the loop moved out of it; keeping the coverage backend keeps the
; measured set intact. Inert without --instrument-with.

(library
 (name windtrap_mutation)
 (public_name windtrap.mutation)
 (libraries unix windtrap windtrap_mutate)
 (library_flags (-linkall))
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage)))
